<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89743" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσμένω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτι-</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			615.7
		</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bide, wait</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνον πολλόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.199
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῖγ᾽ ἔχουσα πρόσμενε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1236
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1399
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσυχάζων π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				620
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. χρόνον ὀλίγον ἔστ᾽ ἂν . . ,
				π. ἕως . . </span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.4.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat.,
				<i>remain attached to, cleave to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθεα π. τοκεῦσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					497
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ Κυρίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					11.23
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ταῖς δεήσεσιν</span>
			<i>continue in . . </i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
				5.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ἑαυτῶν ἀγωγαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.436
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>wait for, await</i>, c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1144
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				837
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				164
			</span></i>(lyr.), etc.; <i>face</i> in battle, <i>stand one's ground
				against</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δορίκτυπον ἀλαλάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					3.60
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. et inf.
			fut., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρέστην τῶνδε προσμένουσ᾽ ἀεὶ
					παυστῆρ᾽ ἐφήξειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					303
				</span></i>
			.</div>
